NAME
       nmtui - text menus for NetworkManager settings

SYNOPSIS
       nmtui [edit [NAME] | connect [NAME] | hostname [NAME]]
       nmtui-edit [NAME]
       nmtui-connect [NAME]
       nmtui-hostname [NAME]

DESCRIPTION
       nmtui is a full-screen menu program for the terminal. It changes the
       same NetworkManager connection profiles as nmcli, but you move with the
       arrow keys and Tab, choose with Enter and type values into fields.
       Some people find it easier than nmcli for a first static address.

       Started with no arguments it offers three tasks:

       Edit a connection
              Add, change or delete a profile: addresses (with prefix, such
              as 192.168.50.11/24), gateway, DNS servers, search domains and
              "Automatically connect".

       Activate a connection
              Start or stop a profile on its device.

       Set system hostname
              Change the static host name.

       The program names nmtui-edit, nmtui-connect and nmtui-hostname jump
       straight to one of these tasks. As with nmcli, a changed profile is
       used after it is activated again (deactivate and activate it in
       nmtui, or run "nmcli connection up NAME").

       nmtui is in the NetworkManager-tui package.

EXAMPLES
              # nmtui
              # nmtui-edit enp1s0
              # nmtui-hostname

NOTES
       Cert Lab's terminal does not draw full-screen menus: use nmcli for the
       same settings there.

SEE ALSO
       nmcli(1), hostnamectl(1)
